From 3915a57f6eed2d16e253b86205877a1f5de8de8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:45:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: only real use stamps the remote warm set
 (reconnect sweep no longer prewarms/holds every listed profile)

After the hub default backend reconnected, the renderer redialed every pooled
hub-profile secondary socket in the same millisecond (reconnectSecondaryGateways
-> reconnectSecondary -> openSecondary -> hermes:connection:for + ws-url-for).
Each was a non-passive ensureRegistryBackend dial, and main counted every such
dial as use: remoteWarmSet.recent.touch + holds.noteUse. So all listed profiles
were stamped with one timestamp (cap-4 prewarm set decided by tie order; bb-tuner
respawned/kept warm with no dispatch) and each got a 30-min keep-alive hold.

Now a dial counts as use only when its caller says so (opts.use: terminal opens).
Renderer user actions report use through a new hermes:remote:note-use IPC
(store/remote-use, throttled 1/min per scope): foreground open/create/request
(spawnPriority 'foreground'), a user-chosen profile activation, and a routed
prompt.submit turn (including sends on a remote primary). Socket (re)dials,
ws-url mints, session-list/roster reads, passive reads and the prewarm probe
never count. Caps and thresholds unchanged.

Tests: electron/remote-warm-use.test.ts (sweep of N profiles touches neither the
recent set nor the hold; real use does both; main wiring), src/store/
gateway-remote-use.test.ts (post-reconnect sweep of 4 pooled hub profiles redials
each with no note-use; foreground open/create/retain and prompt.submit do).
